<article class="env-definition" id="F94EFD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F94EFD">Definition <span data-tag="F94EFD">2.1.1.1</span>.</a>category!cofibered in groupoids Let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a functor between categories. We say that <em>$\calC $ is cofibered in groupoids over $\calD $</em> if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
For every object $C \in \calC $ and every morphism $\eta : F(C) \rightarrow D$ in $\calD $, there exists a morphism $\widetilde{\eta }: C \rightarrow \widetilde{D}$ such that $F(\widetilde{\eta }) = \eta $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every morphism $\eta : C \rightarrow C'$ in $\calC $ and every object $C'' \in \calC $, the map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \Hom _{\calC }(C',C'') \rightarrow \Hom _{\calC }(C,C'') \times _{ \Hom _{\calD }(F(C), F(C'')) } \Hom _{\calD }(F(C'), F(C'')) \]
</div>
<p>
 is bijective. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>